# CHIP-9 TREATY golden vectors — the F# oracle locks the color-plane semantics (Fn01 / per-plane DRW / selective CLS).
# Format: rom<TAB><hex> · plane<TAB><mask> · 32 rows × 64 hex color digits (colorAt masks 0..7). Conformers: C#/TS/Rust replay the rom and must emit these bytes exactly.
#
# DRW EDGE SEMANTICS (B-1031, locked 2026-06-13): the sprite ORIGIN wraps modulo the 64×32 screen,
# then individual pixels CLIP at the right/bottom edge — pixels are NOT wrapped around. A clipped
# pixel is never drawn and never collision-checked (VF counts collisions only on drawn pixels).
# This is the COSMAC VIP reference behavior (Joseph Weisbecker's VIP, 1977; Langhoff's CHIP-8
# guide; the chip8-test-suite "clipping" quirk). This ROM exercises right/bottom/corner clips, a
# COLOR-PLANE edge draw, the VF COLLISION branch (so clip-vs-wrap is locked on the FLAG, not only
# the display — a marker row at y=24 is drawn iff the edge draw did NOT collide, i.e. clip/VF=0),
# and a DXY0 (n=0) draw-nothing. Sprite at 0x300 = a solid 8×8 block (0xFF × 8 rows).
rom	a300603c6a02d0a860026a1cd0a8603c6a1cd0a860006a0cd0a1603cd0a16c006d183f01dcd1f601603c6a12d0a1f101d0a0
plane	1
